From: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ecm_interface: no MLO bonds on the mainline bonding driver

bond_is_mlo_device() comes from QSDK's bonding driver, which adds bonds of
Wi-Fi 7 multi-link devices. The mainline driver has no such bonds, so with
LAG support enabled every bond is an ordinary link aggregate.
---
--- a/ecm_interface.c
+++ b/ecm_interface.c
@@ -53,6 +53,15 @@
 #endif
 #ifdef ECM_INTERFACE_BOND_ENABLE
 #include <net/bonding.h>
+
+/*
+ * MLO bonds are a QSDK bonding-driver extension for Wi-Fi 7 multi-link
+ * devices; the mainline bonding driver has none.
+ */
+static inline bool bond_is_mlo_device(struct net_device *bond_dev)
+{
+	return false;
+}
 #endif
 #if defined(ECM_DB_XREF_ENABLE) && defined(ECM_BAND_STEERING_ENABLE)
 #include <linux/if_bridge.h>
